  "context_pill": "Domestic Company Tax & Marginal Relief",
  "example_summary": "Computing Marginal Relief for Y Ltd. for A.Y. 2026-27 where total income is ₹ 10,01,00,000 and P.Y. 2023-24 turnover was ₹ 410 Crore.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Tax Rates & Surcharge Matrix for Domestic Companies\n\n| Total Income Threshold | Base Tax Rate (Turnover > ₹400 Cr in P.Y. 2023-24) | Base Tax Rate (Turnover ≤ ₹400 Cr in P.Y. 2023-24) | Surcharge Rate |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Up to ₹ 1 Crore** | 30% | 25% | Nil |\n| **> ₹ 1 Crore up to ₹ 10 Crore** | 30% | 25% | 7% |\n| **Exceeding ₹ 10 Crore** | 30% | 25% | 12% |\n\n*Note: Health and Education Cess @ 4% is levied on aggregate of Income Tax and Surcharge across all slabs.*\n\n### Statutory Conditions & Marginal Relief Checklist\n\n- **Turnover Benchmark Test**: The concessional base rate of 25% applies only if the total turnover/gross receipts in the specified previous year (P.Y. 2023-24 for A.Y. 2026-27) does not exceed ₹ 400 Crore.\n- **Marginal Relief Condition**: Available when Total Income marginally exceeds ₹ 1 Crore or ₹ 10 Crore, where the additional tax payable exceeds the excess income.\n- **Cap on Tax Payable**: Tax payable (inclusive of Surcharge) cannot exceed tax payable on the threshold amount (₹ 1 Cr or ₹ 10 Cr) plus the excess Total Income over that threshold.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Marginal Relief Formula (at ₹ 10 Crore Threshold):  \n> `Marginal Relief = Tax (incl. Surcharge) on Total Income - [Tax (incl. Surcharge) on ₹ 10 Crore + (Total Income - ₹ 10 Crore)]`",
